  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A brief passing shower possible early this morning. \nOtherwise...dry and very pleasant weather today and Tue. Highs in \nthe 70s today and mainly upper 60s to the lower 70s Tue. Lows \ntonight and Tue night mainly in the 40s to the lower 50s.\n\nA cold front crosses the region early this morning with perhaps a \nbrief passing shower. It will result in the remaining fog\nquickly scouring out. Otherwise...dry and very pleasant weather\nis on tap for the region today into Tue. Skies quickly become \nsunny this morning and with the mild start expect high \ntemperatures to reach well into the 70s this afternoon...But \nwith low humidity. N-NW winds will be a bit breezy on the order \nof 20-25 mph with perhaps a few gusts near 30 mph...but still a \nbeautiful day of weather is on tap. \n\nHigh pressure builds in from the west tonight allowing for \ndiminishing winds...but it will remain a bit breezy on the \nCape/Nantucket. Low temperatures tonight will be cool in the 40s to \nthe lower 50s. Sunshine on Tue with cooler high temperatures mainly \nin the upper 60s to the lower 70s...but its possible parts of the \nimmediate eastern MA coast only see highs reach the middle 60s. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Above normal temps return Wed through the end of the \nweek with high temps mainly in the 70s to near 80. A few showers \npossible sometime late Thu into early Fri...But dry weather \ndominates.\n\nUpper trough shifts east of the region allowing warmer mid level air \nto advect in from the west. This will bring a return to above normal \ntemperatures in the Wed through Fri time frame. High temperatures \nwill be mainly in the 70s to near 80. A shortwave/cold front may \nbring a few showers to the region sometime late Thu into early Fri. \nHowever...a dry/tranquil weather pattern will dominate most of the \nweek.",
